  "notes": "Cause code TBD/provisional per FORM-366 header; narrative attributes trip to a combination of two concurrent conditions (test-induced 2B channel trip plus a transient 2NI-5 signal spike causing a momentary 2A channel trip). Modeled as two parallel FailureModes converging on the 2/4 logic satisfaction, per rule 5. SSF RCMUP being out of service is discussed only in Safety Analysis as a pre-existing OOS condition unrelated to the trip's causal chain; not modeled as System/backup since it did not participate in mitigating this failure chain. One main steam relief valve failing to fully reseat is a minor post-trip observation not part of the causal chain to the trip itself; omitted per scope guidance (event is the reactor trip, not the relief valve issue). No block_13 data was reported (component failure table marked N/A), consistent with no equipment failure identified as root cause."
